dialect grammar
grammar stdio.md.mutations
extension md
start document

# P2-FG1: real one-line `OpText::print_op`/`parse_op` shape ALREADY emitted by
# `../../🦀️component.rs` (`print_md_mutation`/`parse_md_mutation`, F6's hand-rolled `keyword
# arg=value ...` convention) -- replaces the pre-Phase-2 ABNF placeholder that described a
# serde-JSON `MdMutation` wire struct the Rust codec never emits (F6 moved every stdio op codec to
# this text shape, see that file's own `#region OpCodecs` doc comment). Every keyword/field-name
# token below is copied verbatim from the real `format!(...)` call sites, not invented.
#
# `hex` (bare `hex`, deliberately NOT defined as a production here) is the framework's built-in
# `hex` MACRO (`📖️grammar/🦀️component.rs`'s `default_macros`/`macro_hex_ok`) -- see the recipe's §3
# pitfall #2 / json's own sibling grammar for why this MUST be the macro and never a hand-rolled
# `{INT|IDENT}*` production (no backtracking, and a `<digits>e<digits>` hex run lexes as one `FLOAT`
# token instead of alternating `INT`/`IDENT`). `Symbol::Ref`'s production-then-macro fallback routes
# a bare `hex` reference here automatically.
#
# `md-block`/`md-inline` mirror `enc_block`/`enc_inline`'s tag-prefixed shape 1:1
# (`../../🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs`'s `#region 🔖️BlockCodec`/`#region 🔖️InlineCodec` -- reused
# `pub(crate)` by this artifact's mutations codec rather than duplicated, per that file's own doc
# comment) and are genuinely, mutually recursive: `md-block`'s `L`(List)/`N`(BlockQuote) arms
# reference `item-list`/`block-list` which reference `md-block` back; `md-inline`'s
# `B`(Emphasis)/`C`(Strong)/`E`(Link) arms reference `inline-list` which references `md-inline`
# back. Exercised end-to-end (both directions, multiple nesting depths) by this wave's own
# `ops_grammar_conformance_law` against real `print_op` output for every `MdMutation` variant,
# `⚙️engine/🦀️component.rs`'s `demo_mutation_cases()`.
document = no-mutation | set-snapshot | insert-block | remove-block | replace-block | set-inlines

no-mutation = "no-mutation"
set-snapshot = "set-snapshot" "snapshot" "=" snapshot-lit
insert-block = "insert-block" "path" "=" path "index" "=" INT "block" "=" md-block
remove-block = "remove-block" "path" "=" path "index" "=" INT
replace-block = "replace-block" "path" "=" path "index" "=" INT "block" "=" md-block
set-inlines = "set-inlines" "path" "=" path "index" "=" INT "inlines" "=" inline-list

# `enc_path`/`dec_path` (`../../🦀️component.rs`) -- `[Y[hex(index)]|Z[index,item],...]`. Every
# comma-joined list in this file (no trailing comma, per `Vec::join(",")`) is modeled as `item*`
# where `item` swallows its own OPTIONAL trailing comma (recipe §1.4's own pattern) -- naturally
# handles the empty-list case (`Star` matches zero occurrences) with no special-case production.
path = "[" path-item* "]"
path-item = path-step ","?
path-step = "Y" "[" INT "]" | "Z" "[" INT "," INT "]"

# `enc_md_snapshot`/`dec_md_snapshot` -- `[hex(schema),block-list]`.
snapshot-lit = "[" hex "," block-list "]"

# `enc_inline`/`dec_inline`, tag range A-I (declaration order, see `../../🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs`'s
# own file doc comment for the full tag-vocabulary table). ONE physical line per production (recipe
# §3 pitfall #4 -- `parse_sequence` stops at the first `Newline` token, no line-continuation syntax).
md-inline = "A" "[" hex "]" | "B" "[" inline-list "]" | "C" "[" inline-list "]" | "D" "[" hex "]" | "E" "[" inline-list "," hex "," opt-hex "]" | "F" "[" hex "," hex "," opt-hex "]" | "G" "[" "]" | "H" "[" "]" | "I" "[" hex "]"
inline-list = "[" inline-item* "]"
inline-item = md-inline ","?

# `enc_block`/`dec_block`, tag range J-P (declaration order).
md-block = "J" "[" INT "," inline-list "]" | "K" "[" inline-list "]" | "L" "[" bool-lit "," opt-int "," bool-lit "," item-list "]" | "M" "[" opt-hex "," hex "]" | "N" "[" block-list "]" | "O" "[" "]" | "P" "[" hex "]"
block-list = "[" block-item* "]"
block-item = md-block ","?
item-list = "[" item-item* "]"
item-item = block-list ","?

# `enc_bool`/`dec_bool` -- bare `"0"`/`"1"` (NOT wrapped in `encode_option`'s `[0]`/`[1,x]` tagging,
# unlike `opt-int`/`opt-hex` below -- `MdBlock::List.ordered`/`.tight` are plain `bool`, not
# `Option<bool>`).
bool-lit = "0" | "1"

# `encode_option`/`decode_option` -- the uniform `[0]` (`None`)/`[1,x]` (`Some(x)`) tag (recipe
# §1.4's tri-state pattern, single-level here -- `MdBlock::List.start: Option<u32>`,
# `MdBlock::CodeBlock.info: Option<String>`).
opt-int = "[" "0" "]" | "[" "1" "," INT "]"
opt-hex = "[" "0" "]" | "[" "1" "," hex "]"
